The jungle here is deep and dark, dew from the canopy falls in light showers
upon your head here. Thick and ancient vines descend and impede any further
progress into the jungle, as if they may in fact be consciously detaining you
here. Such thoughts are of course nonsense, but you remain and consider them.
Northeast you can see great stone pillars among the trees, tall walls block
you from approaching but there does seem to be a clearing north of you that
may perhaps grant a better vantage point. To the west, the grand and stately
palace of Casimir is almost entirely hidden from view.
